<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Cervical screening and sexual-health tests are due, and dental care is overdue. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Opioid use disorder on buprenorphine (F11.20)</content>. Six weeks without opioid use since the plan was adjusted; no gaps in buprenorphine. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; she has naloxone, test strips, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline saved in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue buprenorphine with naloxone 16 mg daily.</item><item>Six-month recovery review in seven weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder on acamprosate (F10.20)</content>. Drinking much reduced; AUDIT-C 3. [S]<list><item>Continue acamprosate and thiamine; PEth and liver tests at six months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No result on record; cytology with HPV testing collected today; every five years if normal</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Offered because of new partners in the past year; urine test today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Syphilis screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Offered with the other sexual-health tests; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>All nonreactive at intake; repeat yearly while any drug use continues</td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy intention and contraception</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not planning a pregnancy; uses condoms; other methods discussed and she will think about them. Buprenorphine is safe to continue in pregnancy, and she was told so</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe at home</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 6, down from 11 six weeks ago; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 3, from 8 at intake; in treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Declined</td><td>About five cigarettes a day; nicotine replacement and counseling offered; she is not ready and will say when she is</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Diabetes screening begins at 35 for adults who are overweight; statin assessment begins at 40</td></tr><tr><td>Breast and colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begin at 40 and 45</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis A vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Dose 2 at the six-month visit</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series complete</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 at intake, recommended for adults with alcohol use disorder</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza vaccine at the six-month visit; COVID-19 vaccine discussed and she will decide then</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision-making for adults 27 to 45; she chose not to have it</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Referred</td><td>Visible decay and no dental visit in several years; dry mouth from buprenorphine discussed; dental appointment arranged</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month recovery review in seven weeks, with PEth, liver tests, blood count, the second hepatitis A dose, and the influenza vaccine. Sexual-health and cervical screening results by phone, as she asked. Dental appointment arranged. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1948-10-19: six-month recovery, alcohol, liver, and mood review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
